{"term":"summary","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:30f15561da3bb449c3","definition":"Concise, brief, or presented in a condensed form; presenting information in such a form.","example":"Near-synonym: abstractive","pos":"adj","synonyms":["summative","summarizing[participial adjective|part. adj.]]>","abstractive"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["summarily","summariness","summary court-martial","summary dismissal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/summary#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:37835e18c67c5823fe","definition":"Performed speedily, without formal ceremony, and (especially) without regard to legality.","example":"Near-synonym: extrajudicial","pos":"adj","synonyms":["extrajudicial"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["summarily","summariness","summary court-martial","summary dismissal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/summary#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:368a213d4b3b554267","definition":"Performed by omitting the procedures of a full trial, but within a legally valid framework.","example":"The matter was brought to a close by summary dismissal of the cases.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["summarily","summariness","summary court-martial","summary dismissal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/summary#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:652f1bd92187189099","definition":"An abstract or a condensed presentation of the substance of a body of material.","example":"I'd forgotten what happened in the first Harry Potter book so I read a summary of the narrative before starting the secon